{
 "description": "Contract cases for the category list, version 2 (INT-008, AC-1, AC-2, AC-6, AC-42, C-1, C-3, C-6, C-11, C-16). One file shared by category_policy, the agent and the api. 'normalise' rows give the expected comparison key of a name; 'label' rows the Gmail label of a name. 'category' rows validate one category: 'existing' are the names already on the list, 'labels' the Gmail labels that exist (the caller's view) and 'adoptable' the subset of them that belongs to an older category, which a new category of the same name adopts instead of clashing; 'rules' is the exact list of refusal rule ids in reporting order, empty means valid. A name of the form __label_len_N__ stands for a valid nested name whose label (Assistant/ plus the name) has N characters; a description of the form __N__ stands for N letters. 'list' rows validate a whole list; 'problems' is a list of [index, rule] pairs, index null for a rule about the whole list; 'generate' N stands for N valid categories. 'instructions' rows give the length of the general instructions (N letters) and the exact refusal rule ids. Invisible characters and look-alikes use unicode escapes.",
